{"label":"concave","explanation":"We have f(x) = 1 / ((7/4) + e^x) on [-1,1]. Compute derivatives: f'(x) = -e^x / (7/4 + e^x)^2. Differentiating again,

f''(x) = -e^x(7/4 + e^x)^2{}'·(7/4 + e^x)^{-4} + (-e^x)'(7/4 + e^x)^{-2}
       = -e^x·2(7/4 + e^x)e^x·(7/4 + e^x)^{-4} - e^x(7/4 + e^x)^{-2}
       = -2e^{2x}(7/4 + e^x)^{-3} - e^x(7/4 + e^x)^{-2}.
Factor:

f''(x) = -e^x(7/4 + e^x)^{-3}[(7/4 + e^x) + 2e^x]
       = -e^x(7/4 + e^x)^{-3}(7/4 + 3e^x).

On [-1,1], e^x > 0, 7/4 + e^x > 0, and 7/4 + 3e^x > 0, so every factor except the leading minus sign is positive. Hence f''(x) < 0 for all x in [-1,1]. Therefore f is concave and not convex on this interval."}

